  "source_text": "Corporate Banking Payments Policy\n\nTellers can view customer accounts during business hours.\nTellers cannot approve wire transfers.\nManagers can approve payments up to $25,000.\nOnly the CFO may approve payments over $25,000.\nEmployees cannot approve their own expense reports.\nAccountants can read and update the general ledger only from the corporate network.\nAuditors can only read financial records.\nContractors must not export payroll data.\nDeny by default.\n",
